{"name":"Glazed Persimmon","hex":"#d34e36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glazed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of eyes: glistening but not focusing on anything in particular; showing no liveliness.","Having a glaze (a coating)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of glaze"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glazed"},{"term":"persimmon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The orange fruit of any of various species of trees in the genus Diospyros, especially Diospyros kaki (the kaki or Japanese persimmon) or Diospyros virginiana (the wild American persimmon), which is sweet when ripe and astringent when immature.","The tree this fruit grows on, generally one of two species of ebony: Diospyros kaki (Asian) or Diospyros virginiana (North American)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persimmon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Persimmon","blocks":[{"text":"The persimmon is the edible fruit of a number of species of trees in the genus Diospyros. The most widely cultivated of these is the Chinese, Korean, and Japanese kaki persimmon, Diospyros kaki. In 2023, China produced 80% of the world's persimmons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Fuyu_persimmon_fruits%2C_one_cut_open.jpg/330px-Fuyu_persimmon_fruits%2C_one_cut_open.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persimmon","wikidata":"Q29526"},{"title":"Shades of orange","blocks":[{"text":"In optics, orange has a wavelength between approximately 585 and 620 nm and a hue of 30° in HSV color space. In the RGB color space it is a secondary color numerically halfway between gamma-compressed red and yellow, as can be seen in the RGB color wheel. The complementary color of orange is azure. Orange pigments are largely in the ochre or cadmium families, and absorb mostly blue light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w